I'm just re-readin LotR at the moment, and it seems to me the Nazgul in
nethack could be a little closer to the books (or films, if you
prefer). The suggestions below would not only bring them closer to the
book, but they'd make them more of a challenge (they're pretty wimpy
right now).

1 - In the book the Nazgul have poisonous breath. I think some kind of
1-square radius effect (like a miniature stinking cloud) or very
limited-range breath-ray would be the right implementation. That said,
I realise that this is a lot of specialist code to implement poison
breath to a monster that 999 out of 1000 players will only ever
encounter AFTER acquiring poison resistance, so I guess maybe it
wouldn't be worth the effort.

2 - The weapon used to stab Frodo in book 1 was described as "poisoned"
and "cursed". I think the game should reflect this, and I imagine it
would be fairly easy to code. Again, posion isn't an issue to most
characters advanced enough to be meeting Nazgul, but picking up a
poisoned weapon might make a small difference to them.

3 - At Weathertop, Aragorn tells the hobbits that any blade used to
hurt a Nazgul (or at least the witch-king) will be destroyed. I would
translate this into Nethack as follows:
With each successful hit to a Nazgul with a bladed weapon:
- fooprofed weapons (artifact or mundane) lose their proofing, with
hissing and sizzling noises.
- unfooproofed weapons (artifact or mundane) take one corrosion damage
- unfooproofed non-artifacts at maximum corrosion dissolve completely.
- unfooproofed artifacts at maximum corrosion don't.
While I realise that this could be exploited to get rid of unwanted,
cursed wielded weapons (but not the cursed thouroughly corroded
newtbane- muahaha), Nazgul are rare enough that I don't think it would
have an abusive effect on game balance. Also, characters advanced
enough to meet a Nazgul really ought to have a ?oRC or B!oW by now.
This would add a tiny little bit of variety to the 'chuck daggers at
monsters/ walk up to it and stab it to death" that defines the mid-game
for certain classes- even if it's as simple as going back a few levels
to pick up a club or mace or a spare uncursed +0 long- sword you don't
mind getting melted.

4 - Name one of the game's nine Nazgul the Witch-King of Angmar, and
make him slightly more dangerous (better HP and AC) than the others.
Just for flavour, really.

5 - It might be interesting to code in the "cannot be killed by man"
prophecy, so that male human characters can't damage the Witch-King but
I'm not sure about this. There are already benefits to playing female
characters. Then again, anyone can use an amulet of changing, so maybe
it's not such a bad idea. Either way, you'd definitely want an
oracularity to explain it, or even put the information in the
Witch-King's in-game description.
This might be annoying for some players, but I imagine most would find
it an interesting little diversion, as they find they suddenly have to
either get a "oC, a source of polymoprh, pick up a badass pet or find
some other way of fulfilling/evading prophecy.

6 - Did I miss anything?

And yes, NHINLotR, but what other sources do nethack's Nazgul draw
inspiration from?



